      <a class="btn btn-lg" href="{{ appOnWeb }}">Open it on the web</a>
      @endif
    </div>
  </div>
  <figure class="app-hero-shot">
    <img src="/assets/lsu/images/recap-10-1080.webp" srcset="/assets/lsu/images/recap-10-540.webp 540w, /assets/lsu/images/recap-10-810.webp 810w, /assets/lsu/images/recap-10-1080.webp 1080w" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 48vw, 100vw" alt="A runner in a head torch drinks on the loop at night, lit red." width="1080" height="1440" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
  </figure>
</section>

<section id="screens" class="app-section">
  <div class="app-screens app-shell">
    <div class="app-head">
      <h2 class="h2-sm">What you open<br><span class="accent">before you run.</span></h2>
      <p>Two screens do most of the work: the week you are in, and the session in front of you. These are the app's own, on a phone.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="app-phones">
      <figure class="app-phone">
        <img src="/assets/lsu/images/app/calendar.webp" alt="The app's calendar: a week with 4 h 49 min of 7 h 07 min done, and Monday's tempo run with what it asks for." width="780" height="1580" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption><b>The week against the plan.</b> Time, load and distance so far, and what every session is for.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="app-phone">
        <img src="/assets/lsu/images/app/player.webp" alt="A long run in the app: a start button, then the steps, a warm up, six hard and easy intervals and a cool down." width="780" height="1580" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <figcaption><b>The session, step by step.</b> Press start and it calls every interval, with your phone in your pocket.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="feel" class="app-section">
  <div class="app-feel app-shell">
    <div>
      <div class="app-head">
        <h2 class="h2-sm">How it went<br><span class="accent">shapes the next block.</span></h2>
        <p>Your training arrives two weeks at a time. What you log in this block decides the next one, and a coach reads it before anything reaches your calendar.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="app-steps">
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Train</h3>
            <p>Two weeks of sessions from the method your tier is built on. Today opens first, and the calendar shows the block you are in and the weeks behind it.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Log</h3>
            <p>Mark each session done or skipped, rate the effort out of ten and how it felt, and leave a note on it: heavy legs, a bad night, a week that fell apart.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Next block</h3>
            <p>The app drafts your next two weeks from the plan and from how the last two went. Skipped sessions and hard weeks ease the load, an easy block builds on it. An LSU coach reads the draft, changes what they want and approves it.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <figure class="app-note-wrap" style="margin:0">
      <div class="app-note" role="img" aria-label="Example: a runner's note on a session about heavy legs and a busy fortnight, and the changes it brings to the next block.">
        <div class="app-note-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>Next block · 14 days</span><span>Approved</span></div>
        <blockquote aria-hidden="true">"Legs were heavy from the first kilometre. Work is mad this fortnight, I've only really got Tuesday evening and Saturday."</blockquote>
        <dl class="app-diff" aria-hidden="true">
          <div><dt>TUE</dt><dd><del>Intervals, 6 × 800 m</del><ins>Intervals, 5 × 800 m</ins></dd></div>
          <div><dt>THU</dt><dd><del>Hill repeats, 10 × 60 s</del><ins>Easy run, 40 min</ins></dd></div>
          <div><dt>SAT</dt><dd><del>Long run, 28 km</del><ins>Long run, 25 km</ins></dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="app-note-foot" aria-hidden="true"><span><b>2</b> of 9 skipped</span><span>Coach approved</span></div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="app-caption">An example of the kind of change a block brings. The coach has the last word on every one.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="ai-coach" class="app-section">
  <div class="app-shell">
    <div class="app-head">
      <h2 class="h2-sm">An AI coach<br><span class="accent">that explains.</span></h2>
      <p>Ask it about a session, a bad week or a night of poor sleep, by typing or by talking. It reads your training and tells you what it sees. Your coach decides the training.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="app-steps">
      <li>
        <div>
          <h3>Talk</h3>
          <p>Speak for up to five minutes. The note is transcribed on our own server in Germany and the audio is not kept.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <h3>Check</h3>
          <p>The transcript comes back to you first. Fix anything it misheard, then send it. An unsent transcript is deleted after 24 hours.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div>
          <h3>Understand</h3>
          <p>It reads your sessions, effort and training load, plus sleep, resting heart rate and HRV if you share them, and explains the patterns. It cannot add or change sessions. That stays with your coach.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="week" class="app-section">
  <div class="app-shell">
    <div class="app-head">
      <h2 class="h2-sm">The whole week<br><span class="accent">in one place.</span></h2>
      <p>Sessions, recording, recovery and the numbers that show whether it is working, on your iPhone and in the browser.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="app-bento">
      <article class="app-cell app-cell-photo">
        <img src="/assets/lsu/images/recap-12-810.webp" srcset="/assets/lsu/images/recap-12-540.webp 540w, /assets/lsu/images/recap-12-810.webp 810w, /assets/lsu/images/recap-12-1080.webp 1080w" sizes="(min-width: 1080px) 46vw, (min-width: 640px) 92vw, 100vw" alt="A runner in a green hi-vis vest and head torch, lit blue." width="1080" height="1440" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        <h3>A workout player that keeps up</h3>
        <p>Voice cues for every step and what is up next. It records your GPS route with the screen locked, reads a Bluetooth heart-rate strap and shows the session on your iPhone Lock Screen.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell app-cell-card app-cell-wide">
        <div class="app-readouts" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="app-readout"><span>Fitness</span><b>32</b></div>
          <div class="app-readout"><span>Fatigue</span><b>10</b></div>
          <div class="app-readout is-red"><span>Form</span><b>21</b></div>
        </div>
        <h3>Progress you can read</h3>
        <p>Fitness, fatigue and form from every session you log, with weekly load, consistency and how many planned sessions you finished.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell">
        <h3>Today and the week</h3>
        <p>Today opens with the day's sessions, how much of the day is done and a recovery card from whatever you wear. Week lays out all seven days, and every session says who put it there.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell">
        <h3>Strength and breath</h3>
        <p>Tick off sets as you go, with a video for every exercise. Breathwork sessions come with a pacer that breathes with you.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell app-cell-red">
        <h3>Works offline</h3>
        <p>Upcoming sessions are saved on your phone. Train with no signal and your results sync when you are back.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell">
        <h3>Health and recovery</h3>
        <p>Apple Health and Garmin bring in sleep, resting heart rate and HRV, when you choose to share them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell">
        <h3>A note on every session</h3>
        <p>Every session has its own thread. What you write there goes to your coach with your next block.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell">
        <h3>A link for your crew</h3>
        <p>Share a run while it is happening, privately or publicly, so the people in your corner can follow from home.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell app-cell-card app-cell-wide">
        <div class="app-readouts" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="app-readout is-red"><span>Bell in</span><b>60:00</b></div>
          <div class="app-readout"><span>Rounds</span><b>12</b></div>
        </div>
        <h3>Backyard practice</h3>
        <p>Rehearse the format before race day. Pick 3, 6 or 12 rounds on the hour and the clock counts down to the next bell. Aim for about 50 minutes a round, then walk, eat and drink in what is left.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell">
        <h3>Say how today went</h3>
        <p>Today has a microphone. Talk for about thirty seconds about the day's training, with nothing to type.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="app-cell">
        <h3>Level and goal</h3>
        <p>Say where you stand, what you are training for and when your race is. Today then counts the days to the start.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="app-band band">
