        <p>{{ tier.includes }}</p>
      </article>
      @endforeach
    </div>
    <div class="app-actions app-tier-actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/coaching#training">Subscribe on the web</a>
      @if(appListed)
      <a class="app-textlink" href="#download">Or in the app <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      @endif
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="coaches" class="app-section">
  <div class="app-coach app-shell">
    <div>
      <div class="app-head">
        <span class="kicker">For coaches</span>
        <h2 class="h2-sm">Your method,<br><span class="accent">under your name.</span></h2>
        <p>Write down how you coach once. The app drafts every runner's next two weeks from it and from how their last two went, and nothing reaches them until you approve it.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="app-list">
        <li><b>Block reviews.</b> See how a runner's last block went, session by session, then edit, approve or send back the next one.</li>
        <li><b>Methods with history.</b> A public summary runners see, a private methodology only the AI reads, and every edit kept as a version.</li>
        <li><b>Tiers you set.</b> Running, strength or both, published to the app and to the coaching page on this site.</li>
        <li><b>Builders for the work.</b> A plan library, a workout builder and an AI plan builder that drafts a plan from a brief for you to edit.</li>
        <li><b>Plans for one runner.</b> Assign an individual plan to a subscriber, with your reason written down.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn" href="/app/coaches">See the coach tools</a>
    </div>
    <div class="app-stats">
      <div><b>184</b><span>exercises in the library, with your own on top</span></div>
      <div><b>20</b><span>private sources per method that the AI can quote</span></div>
      <div><b>8</b><span>weeks of a runner's training you can review, once they opt in</span></div>
      <div><b>14</b><span>days of their recovery data, under the same opt-in</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="platforms" class="app-section">
  <div class="app-shell">
    <div class="app-head">
      <h2 class="h2-sm">Where it runs<br><span class="accent">and what it keeps.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <dl class="app-spec">
      <div><dt>iPhone</dt><dd>@if(appListed)On the <a href="{{ appStoreUrl }}" class="accent">App Store</a>, with the session on your Lock Screen while you run.@else In testing on TestFlight, ahead of the App Store. The session shows on your Lock Screen while you run.@endif</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Web</dt><dd>The full app in any current browser, and the training panels on <a href="/coaching" class="accent">lastsoulultra.com/coaching</a>.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Languages</dt><dd>English and German.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Sign-in</dt><dd>Your own LSU account, with email and password or a passkey. Add authenticator-app codes for extra protection.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Your data</dt><dd>Training records are stored in Germany. Download your data as CSV and GPX files, or delete your account, whenever you like.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Medical</dt><dd>The app gives training information. It is not a medical service.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="questions" class="app-section">
  <div class="app-shell">
    <div class="app-head">
      <h2 class="h2-sm">Questions</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="app-faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Does a coach see what I log?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Whether you did each session, your effort, how it felt and your notes on it go to the LSU coach who reviews your next block. Your conversations with the AI coach stay between you and it. For one-to-one coaching, contact a coach directly.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What does it cost?</summary>
        <p>LSU Running is €19.99 a month and LSU Running + Strength is €29.99 a month, tax included. Subscribe in the app or on the <a href="/coaching#training">coaching page</a>, and cancel or resume from the Me tab.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How often does my training change?</summary>
        <p>Every two weeks. The next block is drafted from your plan and how the last one went, and it reaches your calendar once a coach approves it. Sessions you have done and your history stay as they are.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can the AI coach change my plan?</summary>
        <p>No. It reads your sessions and, if you share them, your sleep and heart data, and explains what they show. Only your coach changes your training.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need a watch?</summary>
        <p>Your phone records GPS, and you can log any session by hand: duration, distance, average heart rate, effort out of ten and how it felt. A Bluetooth chest strap or a Garmin adds more detail.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens to my health data?</summary>
        <p>The app only reads the health data you allow, and only to plan your training. It is stored in Germany. Read the details in the <a href="https://training.lsu.stacksjs.com/legal/lsu/privacy">app privacy notice</a>.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="download" class="app-doors">
  <div class="app-door">
    <h2>Running the<br><span class="accent">next block?</span></h2>
    @if(appListed)
    <p>Download the app and pick a tier. Your first two weeks arrive once a coach has approved them.</p>
    <div class="app-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-lg" href="{{ appStoreUrl }}">App Store</a>
    </div>
    <a class="app-textlink" href="{{ appOnWeb }}">Already training? Sign in on the web <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    @else
    <p>Pick a tier and train in your browser. Your first two weeks arrive once a coach has approved them.</p>
    <div class="app-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-lg" href="/coaching/plans">Choose a tier</a>
    </div>
    <a class="app-textlink" href="{{ appOnWeb }}">Already training? Sign in <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    @endif
  </div>
  <div class="app-door">
    <h2>Coaching<br><span class="accent">runners?</span></h2>
    <p>Bring your method to the app, approve every runner's blocks and earn from each one who trains with it.</p>
    <a class="btn-outline" href="/app/coaches">Bring your method</a>
  </div>
</section>

</div>
